codex
The candidate claim does execute a body matching `solution.mpy`; the only proof-local operational acceleration I see so far is the negative-index rule for the symbolic `snocVS` tail. I’ll test that rule both with and without the extension and audit its full match domain rather than accepting the comment that calls it “derived.” The supplied semantics also exposes an explicit opaque `sortVS` trust boundary, so the final result’s connection to Python sorting must be accounted for separately.
