Stage 6 behaves correctly: the false empty-result mutation parses/builds, reaches the real return state, then fails with `WarnStuckClaimState` because heap location 1 contains `[]`, not `[0]`. The proof is result-constraining and non-vacuous; the eventual failure verdict is instead about the quantified length≥2 claims not denoting real MPython list states. I’m writing the seven-stage review and trust ledger now.
